{"title":"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the sum of all the angles except one of a convex polygon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690aac80fe0f74795ddebc869e7d522d3a2bd0d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2190^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, then the number of sides of the polygon must be \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472cc98260e2c45e52e0af9222678416b6658973.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 13 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 15 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 17 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 19 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"393\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of sides in the polygon.  The number of interior angles in the polygon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/e/a5eccfe73a52885542fe472750d0ea086d9b33eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180(n-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" />.  We know that the sum of all but one of them is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690aac80fe0f74795ddebc869e7d522d3a2bd0d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2190^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, so the sum of all the angles is more than that.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/9/9d9b325fe94f5d074666d71083d28048ab9c57b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[180(n-2) &gt; 2190\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/6901979cf1e8765a880ea98b13195f03b41e98ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n-2 &gt; 12 \\tfrac{1}{6}\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b64802790b73d74af941cafea28476e7ffca7299.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n &gt; 14 \\tfrac{1}{6}\\]\" width=\"62\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>The sum of the angles in a 15-sided polygon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/0/3c01169ffda7fce6d5aa70756216526275b23fbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2340^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, making the remaining angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/995f44efd3d9791d3844223f8bd6b35c600050fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$150^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />.  The angles of a convex polygon are all less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />, and since adding one more side means adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> to the measure of the remaining angle, we can confirm that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7ea2ce80a9b2e5e7c2e0e88d1d629de42a98cbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> sides in the polygon.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME\" title=\"1973 AHSME\">1973 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1973 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1973\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index